id: rust.tokio-join
kind: rust
title: tokio::join! and try_join!
aliases: join, join_all, concurrent await
tags: async, concurrency
questions:
  - how do you run several async calls concurrently and wait for all of them?
invariant: join! awaits futures concurrently inside one task and returns every result; it never cancels a branch.
answer_30s: join! runs futures concurrently in the current task and waits for all of them: fan-out without spawning and without cancellation.
when_to_use:
  - parallel independent IO with all results required, same task, small bounded set
avoid_when:
  - unbounded collections (bound with buffered or a semaphore) or work that must outlive the caller
failure_modes:
  - join_all over a large collection, which is unbounded fan-out in disguise
  - assuming join cancels siblings on error (that is try_join, and only then)
related:
  - rust.tokio-select
  - rust.tokio-spawn
  - rust.bounded-concurrency
sources:
  - https://docs.rs/tokio/latest/tokio/macro.join.html
